            <ArticleTitle>The effect of morphine and some other narcotic analgesics on brain tryptophan concentrations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An acute dose of morphine increased brain tryptophan in mice. This effect was not prevented by naloxone nor was it produced by other narcotic analgesics. Dextrorphan, but not levorphanol, had a similar effect to morphine. A large dose of tryptophan had no effect on the antinociceptive action of morphine in mice. Morphine increased brain tryptophan in rats. This effect was prevented by naloxone. A large dose of tryptophan antagonised the antinociceptive action of morphine in the rat.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
